.Dd August 4, 2024
.Dt TESTSUITE 3cutlet
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm testsuite
.Nd cutlet standard library
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb testsuite
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ic import Ar testsuite
.Pp
.Bl -inset -compact
.It Ic def Ar testsuite name body
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.test name body
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.assert condition *args
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.assert_fail condition *args
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.fail *args
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A basic framework for software testing.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic def Ar testsuite name body
Creates a new sandbox for testing and runs all the defined tests with in it.
The functions
.Ar test ,
.Ar assert ,
.Ar assert_fail
and
.Ar fail
get linked into the sandbox to define the tests.
The tests are defined in the
.Ar $body
parameter with the
.Ar test
function.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal
testsuite "A Testsuite" {
  import ...

  # Setup up the global test environment here.
  ...

  test "A Test" {
    assert {$value1 = $value2} "A failed message"
    assert_fail {$value1 <> $value2} "A failed message"
    fail "A failed message"
    throw "A failed message"
  }

  test "Another Test" {
   ...
  }
}
.Ed
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.test name body
This function define the tests to be executed.
If the function ends normally the test is considered a success.
There a number of ways to indicate a failed test with the reason.
The testsuite provides the
.Ar assert ,
.Ar assert_fail
and
.Ar fail
for this.
Also a thrown exception will be recorded as a failure.
.Bd -literal
test "A Test" {
  # Possible test failures.
  assert {$value1 = $value2} "A failed message"
  assert_fail {$value1 <> $value2} "A failed message"
  fail "A failed message"
  throw "A failed message"

  # A successful test if we get here.
}
.Ed
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.assert condition *args
If the argument
.Ar $condition
evaluates to false then the test fails with the reason in
.Ar $args .
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.assert_fail condition *args
If the argument
.Ar $condition
evaluates to true then the test fails with the reason in
.Ar $args .
.It Ic def Ar testsuite.fail *args
This fails the test with the reason in
.Ar $args .
.El
.Pp
When all the tests have been run are summary of the results are displayed.
Then the sandbox is cleaned up with all of the tests.
